## What You Can Do

Subject to the MPL-2.0, you may:

- Use ThreatForge ThreatModel for personal purposes.
- Use ThreatForge ThreatModel for commercial purposes.
- Copy and redistribute ThreatForge ThreatModel.
- Modify the source code.
- Create derivative works.
- Integrate ThreatForge ThreatModel into larger software products.
- Combine ThreatForge ThreatModel with proprietary software.
- Build commercial security products using ThreatForge ThreatModel.
- Create and distribute modified versions.

---

## File-Level Copyleft

ThreatForge ThreatModel uses the **MPL-2.0 file-level copyleft model**.

If you modify an MPL-covered ThreatForge ThreatModel source file and distribute that modified version, the applicable source file and its modifications must remain available under the MPL-2.0, subject to the requirements of the license.

This does **not** require an entire application containing ThreatForge ThreatModel to become open source.

A larger proprietary application may contain ThreatForge ThreatModel MPL-covered files together with separate proprietary files, provided the requirements of the MPL-2.0 are satisfied.

